/**
 * #10868 — the football web headline and win history (`footballJourney.ts`) on
 * REAL retained production bodies, through the web authorities the page
 * already uses.
 *
 * FIXTURE — `footballJourney10868.fixtures.json`, generated by
 * `/tmp/fb-gen/make_football_fixtures.py` and round-trip verified against the
 * raw files by `/tmp/fb-gen/verify_football_fixtures.py`: a mechanical
 * extraction of the CONSUMED fields only (its `_header` names every retained
 * member and, per source, every excluded one). Numbers keep their source text,
 * keys their source order. Sources (sha256 verified before extraction):
 *
 *   ramsDetail / ramsHistory   Rams–Bills 14780558, scheduled — probability-movement-v89/raw/
 *                              nfl-pregame-detail.json (1f81fa52…), nfl-pregame-history.json (c32ce440…)
 *   jaguarsLiveDetail / …History  Jaguars–Eagles 14639175, live 7–14 — nfl-14639175-detail.json
 *                              (031d8150…), nfl-14639175-history.json (a5d027c0…)
 *   jaguarsFinalDetail         the same game, final 19–17 — nfl-latest-detail.json (b22f3792…)
 *   bearsT0/T1/T2Detail        Bears–Patriots 14780564, live, three successive reads —
 *                              artifacts/shopper/pass-0575/journey/ev-t0/t1/t2.json
 *                              (fbbbf5b9…, e8b7e966…, b1e075e1…). No history body exists.
 *
 * The Bucs–Steelers final (14966179) is the EXISTING repo fixture
 * `__tests__/fixtures/finalForecast11296.json` key `detail_14966179`, read only.
 *
 * CONSTRUCTED here, and named where used: `now`; the hero pair, from the page's
 * own `resolveProbability` exactly as page.tsx calls it (host emulation); held,
 * stale, undated and interrupted host readings; and TEST MUTATIONS — one-key
 * edits of a retained body to reach a refusal or boundary the capture does not
 * carry. A mutation is never real-game evidence. Jest runs in UTC; clock words
 * are compared through the screen's own formatter.
 */

